course: dictionary
lesson: 14588
title: Pliable: bending and being persuaded
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pliable means easy to bend without breaking. It also means flexible. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «The wire was pliable, so Sam bent it into a star.» Sam bent the wire, so pliable must mean easy to bend.
explain: Look for a word that shows the opposite. «Clay is pliable, but glass is brittle and breaks.» The word but tells you that glass is different from clay. Brittle breaks, so pliable must mean the opposite: it bends instead of breaking.
explain: Pliable can also describe people. «The quiet boy was so pliable that the older boys talked him into trouble.» Here pliable means easily persuaded or controlled by others. The clue is talked him into trouble. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Pliable means easily bent without breaking; flexible.
fact: Pliable materials include clay, wire, rubber and willow.
fact: «Glass» is brittle, so it breaks instead of bending.
fact: About people, pliable means easily persuaded or controlled by others.
fact: Pliable is an adjective: more pliable, most pliable.
exercise: «The wire was pliable, so Sam bent it into a star.» What does pliable mean here? | Very heavy | Too hard to touch | Shiny and silver | *Easily bent without breaking
exercise: «Clay is pliable, but glass is brittle and breaks.» Which material is pliable? | Brittle | *Clay | Glass
exercise: «The quiet boy was so pliable that the older boys talked him into trouble.» What does pliable mean about the boy? | Tall and strong | Bored with school | *Easily talked into doing things by others | Very good at drawing
test: «Willow branches are pliable, so gardeners can weave them into baskets.» What does pliable mean? | *Easy to bend into shapes | Dry and crumbly | Hard to cut | Very tall
test: Why might a pliable person be in danger from bad friends? | *They can be easily talked into doing wrong | They always know the answer | They are too strong to be moved | They never listen to anyone
exam: «The brittle glass cracked, but the pliable clay just bent.» Which word shows the opposite of pliable? | glass | clay | *brittle | bent
